@meta
id: 30-07
title: Read it without leaving
chapter: 30
type: lesson
skills: ctags
par: 44
minutes: 5
vscode: hovering the name, or Alt-F12 to peek
open: src/domain/order/order.resolver.ts

@brief
Half the time you do not want to *go* to the definition. You want to see
its first line, check the arguments, and keep typing where you are.

The resolver hands `cancel` one argument. The provider wants two. Look
up what the second one is without losing the line you are editing, then
pass `args.reason`.

The provider and the tags file are provided and neither changes.

@keys
| `Ctrl-W }` | open the definition of the word under the cursor in the preview window |
| `:ptag name` | the same, by name |
| `Ctrl-W z` | close the preview window |
| `Ctrl-W ]` | open the definition in a normal split instead |
| `:pclose` | the long form of `Ctrl-W z` |

@hints
Get the cursor onto `cancel` at the call site, then `Ctrl-W }`. A small
window opens at the top with the definition in it; your cursor never
moves.
--
`Ctrl-W z` closes it again. Everything in between is ordinary editing in
the window you were already in.
--
`/cancel(args` `Enter`, `Ctrl-W }`, read the signature, `Ctrl-W z`,
`f)`, `i, args.reason`, `Esc`, `:wq`.

@solution
    /cancel(args<Enter>  Ctrl-W }   Ctrl-W z
    f) i , args.reason <Esc>  :wq<Enter>

The preview window is the original hover. It is a real window holding a
real buffer, so you can `Ctrl-W P` into it and scroll if one line was
not enough, and `Ctrl-W z` closes it from anywhere.

`Ctrl-W ]` is the other half of the pair: a normal split, for when you
are going to work in both files for the next ten minutes rather than
glance at one line. The split keeps its own cursor, which makes
"implement the interface" a pleasant job — definition on top, your file
below, `Ctrl-W w` between them.

Both take the same tags file you already have. Nothing new is running.

@start tags
!_TAG_FILE_FORMAT	2	//
!_TAG_FILE_SORTED	1	//
OrderProvider	src/domain/order/order.provider.ts	/^export class OrderProvider {$/;"	c
OrderResolver	src/domain/order/order.resolver.ts	/^export class OrderResolver {$/;"	c
cancel	src/domain/order/order.provider.ts	/^  public async cancel(id: string, reason: string) {$/;"	m	class:OrderProvider

@start src/domain/order/order.resolver.ts
import { OrderProvider } from './order.provider';

export class OrderResolver {
  constructor(protected orderProvider: OrderProvider) {}

  public async cancelOrder(_: unknown, args: { id: string; reason: string }) {
    return this.orderProvider.cancel(args.id);
  }
}

@expected src/domain/order/order.resolver.ts
import { OrderProvider } from './order.provider';

export class OrderResolver {
  constructor(protected orderProvider: OrderProvider) {}

  public async cancelOrder(_: unknown, args: { id: string; reason: string }) {
    return this.orderProvider.cancel(args.id, args.reason);
  }
}

@start src/domain/order/order.provider.ts
export class OrderProvider {
  public async cancel(id: string, reason: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED', cancellationReason: reason },
    });
  }
}
